# Stack

Morphée is a tiny native **C#** Windows 11 utility (no Electron, no Node, no UI).

- **Primary behavior**: on launch, put the PC to sleep (no UI, no prompts, no console window)
- **Source**: `src/Morphee.cs`, compiled as `/target:winexe` so no console ever appears
- **Sleep method**: Modern Standby (S0ix) → turn display off (`SC_MONITORPOWER`), same as Start → Sleep; S3 machines → `SetSuspendState(false, false, false)`. Never fall back to hibernate — it only wakes via the power button
- **Distribution**: single portable `.exe`
- **Do not** treat this as Electron, Angular, React, Next.js, or a web SPA

# Layout

- Source: `src/Morphee.cs`
- Build script: `build.cmd` (uses `%SystemRoot%\Microsoft.NET\Framework64\v4.0.30319\csc.exe`, C# 5)
- Build output: `release/Morphee.exe`
- App icon: `build/icon.ico` (also `build/icon.png`)

# Commands

- `build.cmd` — build `release/Morphee.exe`
- `release\Morphee.exe --dry-run` — detect sleep mode only (exit code 1 Modern Standby, 2 S3, 3 none)

# Conventions

- No windows, no console, no child processes — call Win32 directly via P/Invoke
- Stay within C# 5 (the compiler bundled with Windows)
- Errors are logged to `%TEMP%\morphee-error.txt`
